Package: flp-rulebook
Architecture: all
Depends: swi-prolog-nox (>= 9.0)
Suggests: python3
Description: Inform 7-inspired rulebook engine in Prolog, for life planning
 flp-rulebook collects the rules that apply to an action or activity,
 orders them by explicit priority, and returns structured outcomes
 (block, prereq, advise, warn).  Facts carry a staleness model (sticky,
 live, decay) because a planner's knowledge of the world is partial.
 .
 Layers: the core engine; activities with before/during/after rulebooks;
 export of a decision to HDDL, PDDL or Peleus; and an HTN planner
 round-trip through a vendored copy of PyHOP (needs python3).
 .
 Files are installed in /usr/share/flp-rulebook.  Other programs load
 them through a file_search_path alias; see the README.
